--
Reclassified as KNOWNBUG by the member-alias template-parameter identity fix
(template_map.cpp: a member alias template's own parameter references are no
longer captured by an unrelated enclosing template's argument, per
[temp.local]/1).  That fix makes std::decay / std::__conditual resolve
correctly, which reroutes std::any's _Manager_internal<T> instantiation through
the lazy, ODR-use-driven path.  In that path the static member function
_S_manage's body is not instantiated ("no body for callee
std::any::_Manager_internal<int>::_S_manage"), so the any_cast assertion fails.
This is a pre-existing gap in ODR-use-driven member-function instantiation
([temp.inst]/4 + [basic.def.odr]) that the eager-substitution ("baking") path
happened to hide; it is tracked as Part 2 of the std::decay fix work
(.kiro/part2_findings.md).
